# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Published bundles are evidence. Kept exactly as the agent wrote them, so a
# checkout on any platform is the same file that was signed.
#
# Verification does not actually depend on this: a signature covers the
# canonical re-serialisation of the parsed bundle, not the bytes of the file,
# so a CRLF checkout still verifies (tested). The point is that
# `corpus/2026-08/README.md` claims these are published unmodified, and
# `text=auto` above would quietly make that claim false.
corpus/** -text
